Day 2 – Networking Fundamentals for Cybersecurity

Today's Learning

Today I focused on building a strong networking foundation, which is essential for understanding how systems communicate and how cyber attacks exploit networks.

Topics Covered

What is Networking & Why Cybersecurity Needs It
  - Basics of computer networks
  - Importance of networking in ethical hacking and penetration testing
  - How attackers and defenders rely on network knowledge

OSI Model & TCP/IP Model
  - Understanding all OSI layers
  - Comparing OSI and TCP/IP models
  - Data flow from sender to receiver

IP Addressing, Subnetting & CIDR Notation
  - IPv4 address structure
  - Public vs Private IPs
  - Subnet masks
  - CIDR notation
  - Network and Host identification

Core Networking Protocols
  - TCP
  - UDP
  - DNS
  - ARP
  - DHCP
  - HTTP / HTTPS
  - ICMP
  - FTP
  - SSH

Key Takeaways

- Networking is the backbone of cybersecurity.
- Every cyber attack begins with understanding how devices communicate.
- The OSI and TCP/IP models simplify troubleshooting and attack analysis.
- IP addressing and subnetting help identify devices and network boundaries.
- Understanding protocols is essential for traffic analysis and penetration testing.

Tools Mentioned

- Wireshark
- Ping
- Traceroute
- ipconfig / ifconfig

